1
00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.597
Unit fifteen. Basic Troubleshooting Skills!

2
00:00:05.556 --> 00:00:10.277
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.327 --> 00:00:13.434
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.485 --> 00:00:18.078
Today we learn about Basic Troubleshooting Skills. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.628 --> 00:00:23.517
Troubleshoot. Say it with me. Troubleshoot!

6
00:00:26.998 --> 00:00:31.920
Problem-solving. Say it with me. Problem-solving!

7
00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:39.624
Restart. Say it with me. Restart!

8
00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:47.801
Check connection. Say it with me. Check connection!

9
00:00:51.346 --> 00:00:55.746
Error message. Say it with me. Error message!

10
00:00:59.185 --> 00:01:03.677
Step-by-step. Say it with me. Step-by-step!

11
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:11.571
Diagnose. Say it with me. Diagnose!

12
00:01:15.044 --> 00:01:18.561
Fix. Say it with me. Fix!

13
00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:33.594
Troubleshooting means solving a technology problem step-by-step. I might restart a device, check a connection, or read an error message to diagnose and fix it.

14
00:01:33.644 --> 00:01:37.499
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:38.339 --> 00:01:43.590
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.790
Restart!

17
00:01:45.921 --> 00:01:51.581
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:51.631 --> 00:01:52.861
Diagnose!

19
00:01:54.035 --> 00:02:02.691
Did you know? 'Have you tried turning it off and on again?' is actually one of the most effective troubleshooting tips in real tech support!

20
00:02:02.741 --> 00:02:04.824
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:06.019 --> 00:02:17.112
Think and answer. What is the first troubleshooting step you usually try when technology isn't working?

22
00:02:17.162 --> 00:02:18.316
Great answer!

23
00:02:19.322 --> 00:02:25.191
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
